# Monorepo Package Management Rules

## Package Structure
Plane uses a monorepo with shared packages under `packages/` and applications under `apps/`.

## Shared Package Guidelines
- All shared packages use the `@plane/` namespace
- Packages are built with `tsup` for optimal bundling
- Each package has its own `package.json` with proper exports
- Use `"private": true` for internal packages

## Package Dependencies
- Apps depend on shared packages using `"*"` version (workspace references)
- Shared packages can depend on other shared packages
- Avoid circular dependencies between packages
- Use peer dependencies for React in UI packages

## Build System
- Use Turborepo for build orchestration
- Each package has `build`, `dev`, `check:lint`, `check:types` scripts
- Build outputs go to `dist/` directory
- Use `tsup` for TypeScript compilation and bundling

## Package Development
```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "build": "tsup --minify",
    "dev": "tsup --watch",
    "check:lint": "eslint . --max-warnings X",
    "check:types": "tsc --noEmit"
  }
}
```

## Key Packages
- **`@plane/ui`**: Shared UI components with Storybook
- **`@plane/types`**: TypeScript definitions
- **`@plane/services`**: API service layer
- **`@plane/constants`**: Application constants
- **`@plane/utils`**: Utility functions

## Import Patterns
```typescript
// Import from shared packages
import { Button } from "@plane/ui";
import { API_BASE_URL } from "@plane/constants";
import { formatDate } from "@plane/utils";
import type { User } from "@plane/types";
```